# Remedy AI — Clinical Intelligence for Heart Risk Assessment

Remedy AI is a premium AI-powered clinical decision-support platform built to evaluate cardiovascular risk from structured patient inputs, explain the model's reasoning, and surface safe, actionable guidance for care teams.

It is designed as a serious decision-support system: explainable, operationally clear, and enterprise-ready — not a generic demo dashboard.

> This project is for research and product exploration. It is not a medical device, not a diagnosis, and not clinical-grade risk validation.

## Why this product stands out

- Premium health-tech product feel instead of a default prototype aesthetic
- Explainability-first experience for every assessment
- Trust-building workflow with user review and safe fallback behavior
- Designed as a platform pattern that can scale into clinical operations, not just a model demo
- Clear separation between model output and human medical judgment

## What the system does

- Estimates cardiovascular disease risk from structured assessment inputs
- Explains which features influenced the prediction most
- Produces AI-guided recommendations grounded in health information workflows
- Supports assessment history, report review, and risk tracking over time
- Exposes enterprise-style product patterns: analytics, summaries, risk views, and workflow clarity

## Product architecture

```text
User / Care Team
      │
      ▼
Next.js product UI
  - dashboard overview
  - assessment intake
  - result interpretation
  - history and report flows
      │
      ▼
FastAPI backend
  - auth and session security
  - assessment orchestration
  - guidance and explanation APIs
  - FHIR-ready export paths
      │
      ▼
ML + AI layer
  - model inference
  - feature impact explanations
  - AI guidance pipeline
      │
      ▼
Data & services
  - PostgreSQL / Redis
  - vector-search / knowledge retrieval
  - storage and audit-friendly workflows
```

## Stack

- Frontend: Next.js, TypeScript, Tailwind, shadcn-inspired component system
- Backend: FastAPI, Python, SQLAlchemy, Alembic
- ML: scikit-learn, explainability workflows, calibrated risk models
- Data: Postgres + pgvector, Redis, storage integration patterns
- Product patterns: SaaS dashboard, assessment flow, analytics, secure review UI

## Getting started

### Prerequisites

- Python 3.12+
- Node 22+
- Docker for local infra

### Quick setup

```bash
# Backend
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e ".[dev]"

# Frontend
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev
```

### Full local stack

```bash
docker compose up -d postgres redis
cp .env.example .env
# configure required environment values
```

## Product vision

Remedy AI is meant to feel like a modern clinical intelligence product: calm, precise, enterprise-aware, and built around trust. The interface and architecture are designed to move beyond a raw ML prediction into a workflow where people can understand risk, inspect reasoning, and act with context.

## Repository structure

```text
